{"cell": "all-interpretation", "word": "whole verse", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "whole verse · interpretation", "words": ["*"], "view": "The Joseph story shows God's hidden direction of affairs: people may dislike what benefits them or love what harms them.", "rows": ["ASAD-NOTES:12:intro/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "all-inward", "word": "whole verse", "type": "inward", "topic": "whole verse · inward", "words": ["*"], "view": "Ali compared disciplining his soul to gathering a flock on one side only to have it scatter on another.", "rows": ["TUSTARI:12:42/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-reports", "word": "لِلَّذِى (word 2)", "type": "reports", "topic": "لِلَّذِى (word 2) · reports", "words": ["لِلَّذِى ظَنَّ أَنَّهُۥ نَاجٍۢ مِّنْهُمَا"], "view": "The Torah says Pharaoh jailed the cupbearer and baker after they offended him; Joseph served them, and their dreams came on the same night. The baker's three baskets meant execution after three days.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p45/r1", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p45/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-reports", "word": "لِلَّذِى (word 2)", "type": "reports", "topic": "لِلَّذِى (word 2) · reports", "words": ["لِلَّذِى ظَنَّ أَنَّهُۥ نَاجٍۢ مِّنْهُمَا"], "view": "Al-Tabataba'i rejects an al-Qummi report that makes the two men royal attendants guarding Joseph, contrary to their being prison companions.", "rows": ["TABATABAI:12:41-42#2/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w3-meaning", "word": "ظَنَّ (word 3)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "ظَنَّ (word 3) · meaning", "words": ["ظَنَّ"], "view": "Joseph knew or was convinced the cupbearer would survive; ظن can express certainty, especially if his settled prediction came by revelation. A prophet's definite but false prediction would undermine his message.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r3", "THALABI:v5p224/r4", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r1", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r1", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p243#2/r4", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p246/r9", "TABRISI:12:42/r1", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r2", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r1", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r1", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r2", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r1", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r2", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r1", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r2", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r1", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r3", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w3-meaning", "word": "ظَنَّ (word 3)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "ظَنَّ (word 3) · meaning", "words": ["ظَنَّ"], "view": "Joseph merely expected survival because dream interpretation can be conjectural, based on reasoning, and subject to God's confirmation or annulment.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r2", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r2", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r2", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r3", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p246/r10", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p246/r11", "TABRISI:12:42/r2", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r3", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r1", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r1", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r2", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r1", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r2", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r3", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r3", "DURR-FULL:v4p540/r7"], "note": "Ibn Atiyya says this requires reading Joseph's 'the matter is settled' as the completion of interpretation, not certainty about the future."}
{"cell": "w3-rhetoric", "word": "ظَنَّ (word 3)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "ظَنَّ (word 3) · rhetoric", "words": ["ظَنَّ"], "view": "The imperfect 'he thought' prepares Joseph's request, while ظن can express deference to divine knowledge even when Joseph was certain.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r1", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w3-referent", "word": "ظَنَّ (word 3)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ظَنَّ (word 3) · referent", "words": ["ظَنَّ"], "view": "The cupbearer, rather than Joseph, was the one who expected to survive after hearing Joseph's prediction; the prisoners did not necessarily believe his prophethood.", "rows": ["KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r1", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p246/r12", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r2", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r1", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r1", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r2", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r1", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w3-interpretation", "word": "ظَنَّ (word 3)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ظَنَّ (word 3) · interpretation", "words": ["ظَنَّ"], "view": "Joseph was uncertain whether the prisoners had truthfully reported their dreams, making his prediction conditional.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r4", "TABRISI:12:42/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w5-referent", "word": "نَاجٍۢ (word 5)", "type": "referent", "topic": "نَاجٍۢ (word 5) · referent", "words": ["نَاجٍۢ مِّنْهُمَا"], "view": "The surviving prisoner was the king's cupbearer or wine server.", "rows": ["IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r1", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w6-grammar", "word": "مِّنْهُمَا (word 6)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "مِّنْهُمَا (word 6) · grammar", "words": ["مِّنْهُمَا"], "view": "The phrase can modify ناج or be circumstantial; making it the complement of ناج would wrongly imply escape from the two prisoners.", "rows": ["SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r4", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-grammar", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · grammar", "words": ["ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "On the cupbearer reading, the possessive links Joseph's remembrance to the king through association or an omitted expression about reporting him.", "rows": ["KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r6", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r3", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r7", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r10"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-grammar", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · grammar", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "The annexation in the relevant expression follows the same grammatical pattern as another cited construction.", "rows": ["ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r10"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-referent", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · referent", "words": ["ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "Al-Farra takes 'his lord' here as Joseph's human master rather than God.", "rows": ["FARRA:v2p45#2/r6"], "note": "This differs from the usual Joseph reading, which identifies the Lord as God."}
{"cell": "w7-reports", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "reports", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · reports", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "At the prison door, or on the third day as he left, the cupbearer asked Joseph what to convey, and Joseph asked to be mentioned to the king.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r6", "DURR-FULL:v4p540/r6", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-reports", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "reports", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · reports", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "The Torah account has Joseph interpret the cupbearer's three vine branches as three days until restoration and ask him to remember and free him.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p45/r2", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p45/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph asked the freed cupbearer to tell the king about his innocence and wrongful imprisonment, hoping for release.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r1", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2148#2/r4", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r5", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r5", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:12:41-44/r2", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p243#2/r4", "KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r1", "TABRISI:12:42/r3", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r3", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r2", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r2", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r3", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r9", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r2", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph wanted the king told of his knowledge, dream interpretation, standing, virtue, and character.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r3", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r9", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r5", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph wanted the king informed that his brothers sold him and that the charge leading to prison was unjust.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph made the request privately so the condemned baker would not realize he would be crucified.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph saw this request as a possible route to justice after other routes had closed.", "rows": ["ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph meant to guide the king to faith through the cupbearer; al-Alusi objects that release is the apparent aim, though the faith reading suits Joseph's rank.", "rows": ["ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "For a prophet or spiritual elect, appealing exclusively to God is a higher course even where human help, including help from non-Muslims, is lawful; unbelievers may otherwise gloat.", "rows": ["KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r8", "TABRISI:12:42/r9", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r3", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r7", "ALUSI-FULL:v13p77/r10", "TABRISI:12:42/r10"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph could ask the cupbearer for help, but should have qualified the request by mentioning God, perhaps saying 'if God wills.'", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Reliance on God includes disciplined effort within His limits; distress does not justify unlawful means, and such effort is a test of human life.", "rows": ["ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r7", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r8", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph's earlier rejection of other gods makes reliance on a human appear inconsistent with surrender; al-Razi says reliance on people brings hardship, while reliance on God brings the best result.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r2", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-interpretation", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Ordinary use of a human means does not prove that Joseph relied on it instead of God or deserved blame.", "rows": ["TABATABAI:12:41-42/r7", "TABATABAI:12:42/r7", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v13p77/r11"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-theology", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "theology", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · theology", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "God still praises Joseph, so his request for human help does not support accusations of sexual wrongdoing against him.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-law", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "law", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · law", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Human help against harm or injustice is permissible and can be required; cooperation and examples from Jesus and the Prophet support using available means.", "rows": ["JISHUMI:v5p3652/r1", "KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r7", "TABRISI:12:42/r9", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r14", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r7", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r7", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r8", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-links", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "links", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · links", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Joseph inferred the prisoners served the king from their words about serving wine and calling him rabb.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p107/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-inward", "word": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7)", "type": "inward", "topic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى (word 7) · inward", "words": ["ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ"], "view": "The request signifies seeking stable spiritual existence through love; spirit and heart ascend toward unity but remain veiled by divine light rather than fully annihilated.", "rows": ["QASHANI:12:41-42#2/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w9-meaning", "word": "رَبِّكَ (word 9)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "رَبِّكَ (word 9) · meaning", "words": ["رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Rabb here means a human master; al-Aʿshā's poetry and other Arabic uses attest this sense.", "rows": ["IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p217#4/r1", "IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p217#4/r2", "TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r1", "ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r2", "THALABI:v5p224/r5", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p107/r7", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r2", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r5", "DURR-FULL:v4p540/r5", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r4", "STUDYQURAN:12:42/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w9-referent", "word": "رَبِّكَ (word 9)", "type": "referent", "topic": "رَبِّكَ (word 9) · referent", "words": ["رَبِّكَ"], "view": "The cupbearer's master was the Egyptian king, named al-Walid ibn al-Rayyan in some accounts.", "rows": ["MUJAHID:v1p316#2/r1", "MUQATIL:12:41-42/r3", "TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r1", "TAB-FULL:v13p169#2/r4", "ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r2", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2148#2/r3", "THALABI:v5p224/r5", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r5", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r4", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r5", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:12:41-44/r2", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p243#2/r4", "KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r1", "TABRISI:12:42/r3", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r3", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r2", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r2", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r3", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p43/r9", "DURR-FULL:v4p540/r5", "DURR-FULL:v4p540/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r5", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r2", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r2", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r4", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r1", "STUDYQURAN:12:42/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w9-referent", "word": "رَبِّكَ (word 9)", "type": "referent", "topic": "رَبِّكَ (word 9) · referent", "words": ["رَبِّكَ"], "view": "One report identifies the master as the Aziz rather than the king.", "rows": ["TABATABAI:12:41-42#2/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w9-law", "word": "رَبِّكَ (word 9)", "type": "law", "topic": "رَبِّكَ (word 9) · law", "words": ["رَبِّكَ"], "view": "Reports discourage calling a human master 'my lord' or a person 'my slave'; clearer terms honor divine lordship and human dignity. One argument says Rabb is certainly a divine name while Sayyid's status is disputed.", "rows": ["QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#2/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r6", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42/r7"], "note": ""}
