{"cell": "w10-reports", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · reports", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "The Torah says Pharaoh restored the cupbearer and executed the baker on his birthday as Joseph predicted, but the cupbearer forgot Joseph.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p45/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-interpretation", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · interpretation", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "Both readings may be intended: Joseph omitted an appeal to God, causing the cupbearer to forget him; this indirection gently alludes to Joseph's lapse.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r3", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r4", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-interpretation", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · interpretation", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ"], "view": "Restored royal duties and favor distracted the cupbearer, who gave little attention to Joseph despite recently seeing his signs.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v7p2148#2/r7", "JISHUMI:v5p3652/r2", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r7", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r11"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-interpretation", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · interpretation", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ"], "view": "Satan induced forgetfulness of a virtuous act, delaying Joseph's release in God's wise plan.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r2", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r11", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p172/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-interpretation", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · interpretation", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "The cupbearer reading is supported by his later remembering in 12:45, the permissibility of human help, and arguments about the clause's wording.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r2", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r10", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r9", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42/r6", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247/r2", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r8", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-interpretation", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · interpretation", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "The Joseph reading follows the clause's apparent wording and avoids an omitted phrase; his 'forgetting' can mean leaving the better course rather than an involuntary lapse.", "rows": ["WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r13", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r14", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r7", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p248/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-theology", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "theology", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · theology", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ"], "view": "Satan can distract and impede recall, but only God directly causes forgetfulness or removes knowledge; one source connects this discussion with the verse on abrogation.", "rows": ["KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r5", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116#2/r5", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r14", "STUDYQURAN:7:11/r36"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-theology", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "theology", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · theology", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "Prophets may forget ordinary matters but remain protected while conveying revelation; Joseph's forgetting need not breach that protection.", "rows": ["QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r6", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r10", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r11"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w10-theology", "word": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10)", "type": "theology", "topic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ (word 10) · theology", "words": ["فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ"], "view": "Joseph's sincerity and God's protection rule out a culpable Satanic lapse; ordinary use of means does not prove misplaced reliance, and blame reports conflict with the Qur'an.", "rows": ["ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r9", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r5", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r6", "TABATABAI:12:22-34#31/r4", "TABATABAI:12:41-42/r7", "TABATABAI:12:42/r6", "TABATABAI:12:42/r7", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r4", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r5"], "note": ""}
