{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · reports", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "A narration counts the request among three alleged lapses, alongside desire for the Aziz's wife and calling his brothers thieves; variants add a claim that he had not betrayed the Aziz and Gabriel's reminder of his desire.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r2", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p239#2/r9", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p243/r5", "DURR-FULL:v4p534/r7", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r6", "TABATABAI:12:22-34#31/r3", "TABATABAI:12:42/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · reports", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "Joseph prayed for relief, provision from an unexpected source, forgiveness, firm hope in God, and detachment from everyone else; one report says Gabriel taught such a prayer.", "rows": ["DURR-FULL:v4p542/r8", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · reports", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "One chronology puts Joseph's departure from home at seventeen, then seven years in the well, seven in prison, and seven storing food before meeting his father.", "rows": ["DURR-FULL:v4p542/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · reports", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "A report praises Joseph's patience: he interpreted the king's dream before seeking release and sought vindication before leaving, despite the earlier request.", "rows": ["ABDURRAZZAQ:v2p323#2/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-interpretation", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · interpretation", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "Joseph's request to an intermediary, or failure to appeal to God, prolonged his imprisonment as discipline or punishment.", "rows": ["MUJAHID:v1p316#2/r1", "MUQATIL:12:41-42/r3", "ABDURRAZZAQ:v2p323#2/r1", "TAB-FULL:v13p176#2/r2", "TAB-FULL:v13p176/r1", "TAB-FULL:v13p176/r3", "TAB-FULL:v13p176/r4", "TAB-FULL:v13p176/r5", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2148#2/r1", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r1", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r2", "THALABI:v5p224/r6", "THALABI:v5p225/r2", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r9", "QUSHAYRI:v2p77/r10", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p121/r6", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r10", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:12:41-44/r3", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r3", "TABRISI:12:42/r4", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r8", "RAZI-FULL:v18p115#2/r5", "RAZI-FULL:v18p116/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#2/r3", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r4", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r4", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r2", "DURR-FULL:v4p541/r2", "DURR-FULL:v4p541/r5", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p248/r1", "ALUSI-FULL:v13p77/r10", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r2", "STUDYQURAN:12:42/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-interpretation", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · interpretation", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "God extended Joseph's imprisonment to increase his reward or fulfill a wise plan, without necessarily blaming his request.", "rows": ["ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r7", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r3", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p172/r1", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p172/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-interpretation", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · interpretation", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "Joseph's longer stay shows practical causes cannot work independently of God; God arranged causes in a chain, and human plans succeed under divine wisdom.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r3", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p171/r8", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-4-surah-yunus-10-surah-maryam-19:p172/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-interpretation", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · interpretation", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "The request may have been a slight lapse of spiritual station, bringing longer confinement to perfect Joseph; prophets receive close accounting because of their standing.", "rows": ["ALUSI-FULL:v13p77/r10", "ALUSI-FULL:v13p77/r12", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p248/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-interpretation", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · interpretation", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "Joseph's later insistence on clearing his name before meeting the king may have repaired his earlier reliance on the cupbearer.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v18p121/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-law", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "law", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · law", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "Ibn Ashur infers inadequate prison records and oversight; Islamic law later required judges to review prisoners daily.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-inward", "word": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14)", "type": "inward", "topic": "فَلَبِثَ (word 14) · inward", "words": ["فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "The prison years signify the spiritual journey; later cattle and grain visions signal changes in soul and body. When faculties work through God, confinement ends and subsistence begins, though some ego remains.", "rows": ["QASHANI:12:41-42#2/r5", "QASHANI:12:41-42/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w15-reports", "word": "فِى (word 15)", "type": "reports", "topic": "فِى (word 15) · reports", "words": ["فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ"], "view": "The Torah says Joseph was sold to Potiphar in Egypt, prospered in his home, refused his wife's advances, was falsely accused, and gained the jailer's trust.", "rows": ["BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r4", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r5", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ derives from cutting off a piece; related terms describe cut meat, part of property, and a cutting tool.", "rows": ["ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r5", "JISHUMI:v5p3646/r7", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r2", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r11", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r1", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ means three through nine or a portion below ten, the common or preferred Arabic range.", "rows": ["MUJAHID:v1p317#2/r1", "TAB-FULL:v13p177/r2", "TAB-FULL:v13p177/r3", "TAB-FULL:v13p177/r4", "TAB-FULL:v13p177/r6", "ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r4", "ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r5", "THALABI:v5p224/r9", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r11", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r2", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r4", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r8", "JISHUMI:v5p3646/r11", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r4", "KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r4", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r8", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r14", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r15", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r2", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r12", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r6", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r4", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p265/r4", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r2", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r7", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r3", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v12p278/r6", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r5", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r3", "IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ means three through seven.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r10", "ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r4", "JISHUMI:v5p3646/r9", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r3", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p265/r5", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ means three through five.", "rows": ["ZAJJAJ:v3p111/r4", "THALABI:v5p224/r8", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r13", "JISHUMI:v5p3646/r10", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r17", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ means one through four, less than half a decade.", "rows": ["IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p217#4/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r1", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r16", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r12"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ may begin at one and extend to ten or broadly include numbers below ten.", "rows": ["IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p217#4/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r5", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r6", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r7", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r7", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r15", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p265/r6", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ can extend from three through ten.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r12", "JISHUMI:v5p3646/r8", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r4", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r14"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Other reported ranges include four through nine, five through seven, seven through nine, five through twelve, above five to below ten, and twelve years.", "rows": ["IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r10", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r11", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r12", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r13", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r13", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Biḍʿ occurs with tens from ten through ninety but generally not with hundreds or thousands; one account contrasts it with نيف for one or two and gives the feminine بضعة.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v13p177/r5", "THALABI:v5p224/r10", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r14", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r4", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r10", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r6", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p265/r7", "SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r12"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-grammar", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · grammar", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "بضع سنين functions as a temporal adverb; the noun is reported with either fatḥa or kasra.", "rows": ["SAMIN-DURR:12:42#2/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:45/r12"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Many reports give Joseph seven years in prison; Wahb compares this with Job's seven-year affliction and Nebuchadnezzar's seven years among beasts.", "rows": ["FARRA:v2p45#2/r7", "ABDURRAZZAQ:v2p323#2/r2", "ABDURRAZZAQ:v2p323#2/r3", "TAB-FULL:v13p176#2/r3", "TAB-FULL:v13p177/r1", "THALABI:v5p224/r11", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r15", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r18", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r6", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r7", "KASHSHAF-FULL:v2p445/r4", "TABRISI:12:42/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r18", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r2", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r12", "NASAFI-FULL:v2p190#2/r4", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r8", "BIQAI-FULL:v4p44/r3", "DURR-FULL:v4p541/r6", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r1", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r7", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r2", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r6", "STUDYQURAN:12:42/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "One chronology gives five years before Joseph's request and seven more afterward, twelve in all.", "rows": ["FARRA:v2p45#2/r7", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r19", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r8", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v4p244/r6", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r11", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r4", "RAZI-FULL:v18p117/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r11", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r4", "BAYDAWI-FULL:12:42/r5", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Muqatil reverses those periods: seven years before the request, five more as punishment, totaling twelve and fulfilling 12:35.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:12:41-42/r4", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Reports give Joseph's total imprisonment as twelve years.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r4", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r16", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r18", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r8", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r9", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r2", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Reports give Joseph's imprisonment as fourteen years; the punitive part may be less than the total.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v7p2149/r5", "MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r17", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r18", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r9", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v4p391/r9", "DURR-FULL:v4p542/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r4", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Other accounts give five years in all, two added years, or seven total years with two after the request.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r11", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r2", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:12:42/r6", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r10"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "Al-Alusi says the report of seven additional years after five is unestablished in that wording; established versions merely say Joseph remained as long as he did.", "rows": ["ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-reports", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "reports", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · reports", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Reports about the Romans' victory over Persia have the Prophet question or explain biḍʿ to Abu Bakr or the Companions, with answers ranging from three to seven, seven to nine, or one to ten; Abu Bakr was told to raise his wager.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r8", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v4p227/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r1", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v12p124/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-interpretation", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · interpretation", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "The span may denote Joseph's whole prison stay or only years added after the cupbearer's release or after five earlier years.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v3p39/r17", "QURTUBI-FULL:12:42#3/r11", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-interpretation", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · interpretation", "words": ["بِضْعَ سِنِينَ"], "view": "The phrase leaves the precise number unstated, so one should avoid assigning an exact term amid divergent reports.", "rows": ["ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v6p279/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v12p247#2/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-law", "word": "بِضْعَ (word 17)", "type": "law", "topic": "بِضْعَ (word 17) · law", "words": ["بِضْعَ"], "view": "Ibn Abbas's definition of biḍʿ as three through ten informs Malik's rule concerning claims and oaths.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v3p247/r5"], "note": ""}
